  "submitted_text": "Step 1: The original nonagon has a side length of 2 units. A regular nonagon has 9 sides, so its perimeter is \\(9 \\times 2 = 18\\) units.\n\nStep 2: When we consider the set of all points less than 1 unit away from a point on the perimeter of the nonagon, we add a circular band around the nonagon. This band adds an additional perimeter to the shape \\(S\\).\n\nStep 3: Each side of the nonagon will have a semicircular extension of radius 1 unit added to it. Since there are 9 sides, there will be 9 such semicircles.\n\nStep 4: The circumference of one full circle with radius 1 unit is \\(2\\pi \\times 1 = 2\\pi\\). Therefore, the total length contributed by these 9 semicircles is \\(9 \\times \\pi = 9\\pi\\).\n\nStep 5: Adding this to the original perimeter of the nonagon, the total perimeter of \\(S\\) is \\(18 + 9\\pi\\) units.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{18 + 9\\pi}",
